[size=6][b]Event-PVP-Plugin - Quick Description[/b][/size]

A comprehensive Minecraft plugin that combines [b]custom event management[/b] and [b]PvP wager system[/b] into one unified solution.

[size=5][b]Upgrading to 1.0.9[/b][/size]

You [b]do not need to replace your entire config.yml[/b]! The plugin automatically adds missing settings with default values.

[size=4][b]Important Notes in 1.0.9[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]True i18n Localization for Console & Terminal Output[/b]: All logger, startup/shutdown, and server console messages now respect [font=courier new]settings.language[/font] in all 7 languages via [font=courier new]messages.console.*[/font].
[*][b]Automatic Fallbacks[/b]: Missing keys in custom or partial translation files now automatically display English text via embedded resource defaults instead of failing or printing raw keys.
[*][b]Web Interface Live Server Sync Badge[/b]: Real-time status indicators in the top bar show whether your configuration changes are synchronized with the server ([font=courier new]🟢 Synced[/font], [font=courier new]🟡 Unsaved Changes[/font], [font=courier new]🔵 Saving[/font], [font=courier new]🔴 Out of Sync[/font]).
[*][b]Switchable Lobby Phase ([font=courier new]use-lobby[/font])[/b]: Events can now run with or without a lobby phase. When disabled, players join the event world immediately without needing a separate lobby world.
[*][b]World Regeneration Safeguards[/b]: Redundant double-regenerations are automatically prevented, and [font=courier new]regenerate-event-world[/font] is locked when the world is already set to regenerate globally in [font=courier new]worlds.yml[/font].
[*][b]Zero Hardcoded Messages[/b]: Complete localization audit pass (0 findings across all 9 rules D1–D9).
[/list]

[b]🌍 Multilingual Support: Available in 7 Core Languages[/b] (English, German, Spanish, French, Japanese, Polish, Russian) with 100% key parity and full web interface translation.

[size=5][b]What Does This Plugin Do?[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]Event System[/b][/size]
Host custom server events with:
[list]
[*]Multiple event types (PvP Arena, Capture the Flag, Free-for-All, etc.)
[*]Automated event scheduling
[*]Configurable spawn systems (single point, random, team-based)
[*]Custom rewards for winners and participants
[*]Statistics tracking and leaderboards
[/list]

[size=4][b]PvP Wager System[/b][/size]
Let players bet on PvP matches:
[list]
[*]Challenge other players with item or money wagers
[*]Multiple arena configurations
[*]Pre-configured equipment sets
[*]Spectator mode for watching matches
[*]Match management (draw votes, surrender, timeouts)
[/list]

[size=4][b]Web Interface[/b][/size]
Configure everything through a modern browser interface:
[list]
[*]Edit all YAML configurations visually ([font=courier new]config.yml[/font], [font=courier new]worlds.yml[/font], [font=courier new]equipment.yml[/font], [font=courier new]web-config.yml[/font]) with deep-snapshot precision dirty-tracking
[*]Create events and equipment sets with live preview and server material validation
[*][b]Dedicated 3-Tab Inventory Manager[/b]: Search backups, inspect with authentic Minecraft Canvas & XP bar, 2-step restores, live session/guard monitoring
[*][b]Multiverse World Management[/b]: Create, import, load, unload, delete, and backup/restore worlds directly in the browser
[*][b]Server Resource Pack Textures[/b]: Automatically extracts and displays custom item textures from your server resource pack
[*][b]Web Server Settings[/b]: Configurable port with pre-save safety warning dialog and public URL with automatic dynamic port binding for [font=courier new]/eventpvp webtoken[/font]
[*]Token-based secure access ([font=courier new]/eventpvp webtoken[/font]) with rate-limiting protection
[*][b]Multi-language support: 7 languages[/b] (EN, DE, FR, ES, RU, PL, JA) with real-time synchronization badges
[/list]

[size=5][b]Important Dependencies[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]⚠️ InventoryBackup / InventoryRestore (REQUIRED)[/b][/size]
[b]This plugin requires the plugin [font=courier new]InventoryBackup[/font][/b] (from the InventoryRestore project) and will not start without it — it is listed under [font=courier new]depend[/font] in [font=courier new]plugin.yml[/font], exactly like Vault.

It is the storage behind all inventory safety: the backup taken before a player is teleported into an arena or lobby, the automatic restore afterwards, and the persistent queue that returns an inventory to a player who disconnected mid-match. Requires Paper/Spigot [b]1.20+[/b].

[size=4][b]⚠️ Multiverse-Core (REQUIRED)[/b][/size]
[b]This plugin requires Multiverse-Core[/b] for proper operation and will not start without it — it is listed under [font=courier new]depend[/font] in [font=courier new]plugin.yml[/font]:
[list]
[*][b]World Loading[/b]: Loads event/arena worlds when matches start
[*][b]World Cloning[/b]: Creates temporary world copies from templates
[*][b]World Regeneration[/b]: Resets worlds after events/matches
[*][b]World Unloading[/b]: Unloads worlds to save server resources
[/list]

Both Multiverse-Core 4 and 5 are supported.

[size=4][b]✅ Inventory Management (no Multiverse-Inventories required)[/b][/size]
The plugin manages inventory backups and restorations automatically through [font=courier new]InventoryBackup[/font]:
[list]
[*][b]After a match or event ends[/b], including draws and cancellations
[*][b]After a death[/b] in an arena, on respawn
[*][b]After a disconnect[/b]: the restore is queued persistently and applied on the player's next login
[*][b]After a crash[/b]: open sessions are written to [font=courier new]inventory-guard.yml[/font] and restored on startup
[/list]

[b]Modes[/b] ([font=courier new]settings.inventory-management.provider[/font]):
[list]
[*][font=courier new]auto[/font] (default): Backup and automatic restore through InventoryBackup
[*][font=courier new]none[/font]: [b]Legacy[/b] mode for Multiverse-Inventories (plugin only writes safety backups)
[/list]

[size=4][b]Other Dependencies[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Vault[/b] (Required): For economy integration (money wagers)
[*][b]InventoryBackup[/b] (Required): Inventory backup and restore
[/list]

[size=5][b]Essential Commands[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]For Players[/b][/size]

[b]Events:[/b]
[code]
/event <name> join          - Join an event
/event <name> leave         - Leave an event
/event list                 - Show available events
/eventstats me              - View your event statistics
[/code]

[b]PvP Wagers:[/b]
[code]
/pvpask <player>                                      - Challenge a player (GUI)
/pvpa <player> <wager> <amount> <arena> <equipment>  - Challenge with full setup
/pvpaccept [player]                                   - Accept a challenge
/pvpdeny [player]                                     - Deny a challenge
/surrender                                            - Surrender current match
/draw                                                 - Vote for a draw
/pvp spectate <player>                                - Spectate a match
/pvpstats me                                          - View your PvP statistics
[/code]

[size=4][b]For Admins[/b][/size]

[code]
/eventpvp reload            - Reload all configurations
/eventpvp webtoken          - Generate web interface access token
/eventpvp version           - Check plugin version and update status
/eventpvp debug             - Toggle debug logging (on|on full|off|status)
/eventpvp rescue            - Manage stuck sessions and stranded player return locations
/event <name> start         - Start an event
/event <name> stop          - Stop an event
/event <name> forcestart    - Force start without minimum players
/pvpadmin reload            - Reload PvP configuration
/pvpadmin stopall           - Stop all active matches
/inv <player>               - Inspect and restore player backups via InventoryBackup
[/code]

[size=5][b]Quick Start[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*][b]Install Dependencies:[/b]
[list]
[*]Multiverse-Core (Required)
[*]Vault (Required)
[*]InventoryBackup from InventoryRestore (Required)
[/list]

[*][b]Configure the Plugin:[/b]
[list]
[*]Edit [font=courier new]config.yml[/font], [font=courier new]worlds.yml[/font], [font=courier new]equipment.yml[/font]
[*]Or use the web interface: [font=courier new]/eventpvp webtoken[/font]
[*]Enable optional integrations (AJLeaderboards, DecentHolograms, PvPManager)
[/list]

[*][b]Reload and Test:[/b]
[code]
/eventpvp reload
/event pvparena start
[/code]
[/list]

[size=5][b]Server Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Platform[/b]: Paper/Spigot 1.19+ (InventoryBackup requires 1.20+)
[*][b]RAM[/b]: 4GB+ recommended (depending on world size)
[*][b]Required Plugins[/b]: Multiverse-Core (v4 or v5), Vault, InventoryBackup (from InventoryRestore)
[*][b]Optional / Soft Integrations[/b]: PlaceholderAPI, AJLeaderboards, DecentHolograms, PvPManager
[/list]

[size=5][b]Need Help?[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Check the full [font=courier new]README.md[/font] for detailed documentation
[*]Review configuration examples in [font=courier new]CONFIG_EXAMPLES.md[/font] (or [font=courier new]CONFIG_EXAMPLES_EN.md[/font])
[*]Test spawn configurations using [font=courier new]SpawnExamples.md[/font]
[/list]

[hr]

[b]Remember[/b]: Multiverse-Core, Vault, and InventoryBackup are required dependencies. The plugin will not start without them!
